---
const days = [
  { wd: "Fri", d: "6", what: "Debit at 23:40" },
  { wd: "Sat", d: "7", what: "Day 1" },
  { wd: "Sun", d: "8", what: "Not counted", skip: true },
  { wd: "Mon", d: "9", what: "Day 2" },
  { wd: "Tue", d: "10", what: "Day 3. Report by today", due: true },
];
---
<section id="clerk">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid head">
      <h2 class="h2 c-l6">The Clerk keeps the bank's deadline</h2>
      <p class="lead c-r">Under RBI rules, an unauthorised electronic debit reported within 3 working days costs the customer nothing when someone else committed the fraud. Bank watch works out the date in code. On the last day it reminds the Clerk.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cal after-head" data-days>
      <svg class="hops" viewBox="0 0 1000 90" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path class="ink-line" data-hop d="M100 88 Q200 20 300 88" />
        <path class="soft-line dashed" d="M300 88 Q400 40 500 88" />
        <path class="ink-line" data-hop d="M300 88 Q500 -40 700 88" />
        <path class="stamp-line" data-hop d="M700 88 Q800 20 900 88" />
      </svg>
      <ol class="days" aria-label="Counting 3 working days from a Friday night debit">
        {days.map((day) => (
          <li class:list={[{ skip: day.skip, due: day.due }]} data-day>
            <span class="meta">{day.wd}</span>
            <span class="num d">{day.d}{day.skip && <span class="strike" data-strike aria-hidden="true"></span>}</span>
            <span class="meta">Nov</span>
            <span class="small what">{day.what}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
    <p class="note">Every day but Sunday counts. A bank holiday only moves the real deadline later, so the date shown is never too late.</p>

    <div class="grid after-block" data-stagger>
      <div class="c-l">
        <h3 class="h3">Public posts, published by a person</h3>
        <p class="soft measure gap">When a bank, ride app or railway doesn't answer, the Clerk drafts a short post on X tagging the company. After someone in the family says to post it, the Clerk sends a link that opens X with the text filled in. That person reads it and presses Post on their own account. No agent publishes anything.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="c-r">
        <h3 class="h3">What a draft can never carry</h3>
        <p class="soft measure gap">The Clerk's checker refuses any draft with these in it. Names and addresses can't be caught by a pattern, which is why a person reads every post first.</p>
        <ul class="refuse">
          <li>phone numbers</li>
          <li>email addresses</li>
          <li>account-style numbers</li>
          <li>more than 280 characters</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .gap { margin-top: var(--sp-item); }
  .hops { width: 100%; height: 90px; }
  .dashed { stroke-dasharray: 3 5; }
  .days { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); }
  .days li { display: grid; align-content: start; justify-items: center; text-align: center; padding: 22px 8px 26px; border-left: 1px solid var(--rule); min-width: 0; }
  .days li:first-child { border-left: 0; }
  .d { position: relative; margin-block: 12px 6px; }
  .what { margin-top: 18px; }
  .skip .d, .skip .what { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .strike { position: absolute; left: -10%; right: -10%; top: 50%; height: 3px; background: var(--ink-soft); transform-origin: left; }
  .due .d, .due .what { color: var(--stamp); }
  .due .what { font-weight: 600; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .days li { padding: 16px 4px 18px; }
    .what { font-size: 0.75rem; }
    .hops { height: 56px; }
  }
  .refuse { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 24px 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); max-width: 31rem; }
  .refuse li { padding-block: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); font: 400 0.875rem/1.4 var(--mono); text-decoration: line-through; text-decoration-color: var(--stamp); text-decoration-thickness: 1.5px; }
</style>
